  "result": "Fixed: a child `Context` now takes its own section of the parent's `default_map`, so `default_map={'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` gives `changed` instead of `normal`.\n\nThe cause was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`. It handed the child the parent's entire `default_map`, so the lookup for `name` happened one level too high. It now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nI added `test_group_subcommand_default_map` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It checks that `foo` prints `changed` with the default map and `normal` without one.\n\n`python -m pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_defaults.py -q` passes, 145 tests. The full suite also passes, with 1907 passed, 102 skipped and 1 xfailed.",
